# Codegeist 2026 — Forge conventions

This repo is an Atlassian Codegeist 2026 project built on **Forge**.

## Stack

- Forge CLI (`@forge/cli`), Node.js 20+ (prefer 22.x or 24.x LTS)
- App definition lives in `manifest.yml`
- UI Kit frontend in `src/frontend/`
- Backend resolvers in `src/resolvers/`
- Entry wiring in `src/index.js`

## Workflow

1. Change code → `forge lint` / local checks
2. Iterate with `forge tunnel` when installed on a site
3. Ship with `forge deploy`, then `forge install --demo-site` (or an existing site)
4. Never commit API tokens, `.env`, or scoped credentials

## Product constraints

- Integrate at least one Atlassian capability: Jira, Confluence, JSM, Bitbucket, Teamwork Graph, or Rovo
- Prefer modules that support bonus tracks when they fit the idea (`rovo:agent`, `rovo:mcp`, Teamwork Graph)
- Keep `manifest.yml` permissions minimal and intentional

## Agent behavior

- Prefer official Forge docs and templates over inventing APIs
- Do not invent `app.id` — register via `forge create` / developer console when missing
- Keep hackathon notes in `atlassian_*.md` local-only while they remain gitignored
